  "details": "VRChat Version: 1275\n\nRecently, some YouTube videos cannot be played in VRChat.\n\nIt doesn't look like a yt-dlp problem. Using perfview, I captured the command used to obtain the video URL: `yt-dlp --no-check-certificate --no-cache-dir --rm-cache-dir -f \"mp4[height<=?720][height>=?64][width>=?64]/best[height<=?720][height>=?64][width>=?64]\" --get-url <URL>`. If I pass the same parameters to the VRChat version of yt-dlp, I get back a URL that I can successfully play in VLC.\n\nHowever, the VRChat logs seem to show that VRChat does not understand the output of yt-dlp. It outputs messages like this:\n\n```\n\n 2022.12.12 07:42:00 Error      -  [Video Playback] yt_dlp\\jsinterp.pyc:344: FutureWarning: Possible nested set at position 3\n\n2022.12.12 07:42:00 Log        -  [Video Playback] URL 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0xZi79A2NRU' resolved to 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0xZi79A2NRU'\n\n```\n\nDoes VRChat's video resolving code bail out if it sees any text written to stderr? I tried setting `PYTHONWARNINGS=ignore` but it doesn't have any effect because py2exe [sets Py_IgnoreEnvironmentFlag](https://github.com/py2exe/py2exe/blob/43ee68b0fdf474dcedb1ee68fb1445f1d5a9b023/source/start.c#L252-L253).\n\nKnown unplayable videos:\n\n- https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=By7qcgaqGI4\n\n- https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0xZi79A2NRU\n\n- https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jo3OB0F0Rs4\n\nyt-dlp issue: [yt-dlp/yt-dlp#5749](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/issues/5749). yt-dlp made a change to avoid the message, but since it's just a warning that doesn't impact the normal functioning of the program they are unlikely to make a new release just to get rid of it.",
